{
 "manufacturer": "Johnson Controls",
 "manufacturer_slug": "johnson-controls",
 "model": "VFD68 variable frequency drive (VFD68Bxx / VFD68Cxx, Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "vfd68",
 "short_model": "VFD68",
 "aliases": [
  "VFD68Bxx",
  "VFD68Cxx",
  "VFD68BDC-2C",
  "VFD68CDF-2C",
  "PENN VFD68"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
 "applies_to": "Johnson Controls / PENN VFD68Bxx (200-240 V) and VFD68Cxx (380-480 V) drives on their RJ45 PU port with Modbus RTU selected (P.549 = 1), per the VFD68 Variable Frequency Drives Technical Bulletin, Appendix 4.",
 "summary": "Compact HVAC drive with a Modbus RTU subordinate on its RJ45 PU port. All data are holding registers: reset and parameter-clear commands, a control/status word, the running-frequency command (0.01 Hz), a real-time monitor block (output frequency, current, voltage, power, load factors, PID values, energy), eight fault-history slots with fault codes, and every parameter P.n at register 41000 + n.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 0,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "Even",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "Registers are listed as 4xxxx. The bulletin states the address in the frame is the register number minus 40001 and shows it in examples (41004 is sent as H03EB = 1003)."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "VFD68 Variable Frequency Drives Technical Bulletin",
  "doc_number": "24-7664-3051",
  "revision_date": "2019-08-09",
  "url": "https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/bas/r/PENN-Controls/en-US/VFD68-Variable-Frequency-Drives-Technical-Bulletin/C",
  "pages": "Appendix 4, printed pp. 93-110 (Table 88 communication parameters, Tables 93-104 frame examples, Tables 124-130 register maps and fault codes)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Source is Johnson Controls' documentation portal; the bulletin's PDF attachment is 24-7664-3051.pdf.",
  "Scaling comes from the unit column of Table 126 and the worked examples (H1770 = 60.00 Hz written to 40014; P.4-P.6 read as 6000/3000/1000 = 60/30/10 Hz; 0.5 s written to P.7 as 5).",
  "Parameters: register = 41000 + parameter number for P.0-P.999 (C2-C7 calibration values also have 42xxx/43xxx analog-value registers). Only the parameters whose scaling the bulletin shows or that set up communication are listed; see the drive parameter lists for the rest.",
  "Communication defaults from Table 88: P.117 station number 0 (no reply - must be set 1-247), P.118 = 96 (9600 bps), P.120 = 2 (even parity, 1 stop bit), P.549 = 0 (computer link). The VFD68 parameter table (Table 34) instead lists P.549 = 1 (Modbus RTU) as the VFD68 default, so check P.549 on the drive. Communication parameters can only be set when P.160 = 0.",
  "Operation-mode values for 40010 and the control/status bit assignments can change with P.180-P.182 and P.190-P.192; the bits listed are the initial settings.",
  "PID Deviation (40254, 0.1 %) is left out: a deviation can be negative but the bulletin does not say whether the register is signed."
 ],
